# Audeo Release Notes

## 0.2.0 (31 Jan 2026)

### 🎉 Major Features
- **🚀 Asynchronous Download Processing**: Complete rewrite of download submission to prevent UI blocking
- **📁 Direct Folder Access**: Added "Fichier" button in download history to open destination folder directly
- **🔄 Improved Error Handling**: Enhanced error dialogs with thread-safe notifications

### 🆕 New Features
- **Non-Blocking Playlist Detection**: Playlist detection now runs in background thread
- **Cross-Platform File Explorer Integration**: 
  - Windows: Native Explorer integration
  - macOS: Finder integration  
  - Linux: Multiple file manager support (Nautilus, Dolphin, Thunar, etc.)
- **Smart Error Dialogs**: Replaced in-card error messages with native system dialogs
- **Real-time Progress Animation**: Improved ActivityIndicator with proper start/stop methods

### 🔧 Improvements
- **UI Responsiveness**: 
  - Eliminated UI freezing during playlist detection
  - Immediate visual feedback with progress animations
  - Asynchronous task creation and card updates
- **Error Management**:
  - Thread-safe error dialog notifications
  - Early error termination to prevent cascading failures
  - Cross-platform file browser fallbacks
- **Download History**:
  - Simplified file path resolution using destination folder
  - No more temporary file tracking issues
  - Direct folder access functionality

### 🐛 Bug Fixes
- Fixed UI blocking during playlist detection and processing
- Resolved ActivityIndicator deprecation warnings (replaced .running with .start()/.stop())
- Fixed temporary file path issues in download history
- Corrected cross-platform file explorer integration
- Improved error dialog thread safety

### 📦 Technical Changes
- Refactored `DownloadManager.submit()` for asynchronous operation
- Added callback system for async task creation (`_on_tasks_ready`)
- Simplified download history file path resolution
- Enhanced cross-platform compatibility for file operations
- Improved ActivityIndicator usage following Toga best practices

### 🔨 Development
- Added comprehensive logging for debugging async operations
- Enhanced error messages with actionable solutions for Linux users
- Improved code organization for better maintainability
- Added fallback mechanisms for various Linux file managers

---

## 0.1.0 (20 Jan 2026) pre-release

### 🎉 Major Features
- **📋 Video Information Tab**: Transformed queue view into comprehensive video information explorer
- **🔍 Metadata Extraction**: Extract detailed video information without downloading
- **📊 Format Analysis**: Display available formats with resolution, codec, and file size details
- **⚡ Direct Download**: Launch downloads directly from information view

### 🆕 New Features
- **Video Info View**: Complete redesign of queue functionality
  - URL input and analysis interface
  - Detailed metadata display (title, duration, uploader, views, date, description)
  - Interactive formats table with sorting by quality
  - One-click download from analysis results
- **Proxy Support**: Enhanced proxy configuration for both analysis and downloads
  - Proxy settings in preferences
  - Automatic proxy detection and application
  - Support for authenticated proxies

### 🔧 Improvements
- **UI Enhancements**: 
  - Updated navigation icons (info icon for information tab)
  - Improved finished downloads layout with centered clear button
  - Enhanced thumbnail handling with default-200.png
- **Build System**: 
  - Added version.txt for Windows executable metadata
  - Integrated version information in PyInstaller build process
  - Updated build scripts for better resource management

### 🐛 Bug Fixes
- Fixed proxy URL parsing and authentication
- Improved error handling in video analysis
- Enhanced download manager proxy integration
- Corrected navigation references throughout application

### 📦 Technical Changes
- Renamed `QueueView` to `VideoInfoView` for clarity
- Updated import statements and references
- Refactored proxy handling into dedicated utility method
- Enhanced settings structure for proxy configuration

### 🔨 Development
- Updated project documentation
- Improved code organization and comments
- Enhanced error messages and user feedback
- Added comprehensive logging for debugging

---

